      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why rust_ffi_static but not rlib?",
      "revId": "45ab4f6158c89d509e257be39e29da2d001a81bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f59d4eb_56c5e6e3",
        "filename": "rust/image.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-02T14:34:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t support rust vendor binaries or libraries with this CL, so there isn\u0027t anything on vendor that would use rlibs unless I\u0027m mistaken.",
      "parentUuid": "0d429e0a_dcb7be8b",
      "revId": "45ab4f6158c89d509e257be39e29da2d001a81bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74c1f9ac_6beea6c6",
        "filename": "rust/image.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-02T17:28:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The piece I\u0027m unsure about here is that it seems extremely likely that a `rust_ffi_static` module would have at least one `rust_library_rlib` dependency, and that dependency would have to be vendor available. We don\u0027t want to install rust `dylib`s due to the ABI issue, and we want to delay allowing `cdylib`s for the moment, but I don\u0027t see any real issues with making `rlib` or binary files available.\n\nBinary files might be a bit of extra code for installation, but `rlib` should be free since it would only show up by link.\n\n(feel free to re-resolve, just wanted to make sure this was read)",
      "parentUuid": "7f59d4eb_56c5e6e3",
      "revId": "45ab4f6158c89d509e257be39e29da2d001a81bf",
